---
import BaseLayout from "~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Section from "~/components/Section.astro";
import CardGrid from "~/components/CardGrid.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="About · ShedOS" description="ShedOS is an operating system for software developers — a configured tiling desktop and toolchain, on a system you can change freely and always take back.">

  <!-- intro -->
  <section class="hero grid-bg">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:52rem;text-align:center;padding-top:4.5rem;padding-bottom:3.5rem;">
      <span class="eyebrow no-rule" style="justify-content:center;">About</span>
      <h1 style="margin-top:1rem;font-size:clamp(2.2rem,5.5vw,3.4rem);">An OS that's ready, yours, and recoverable.</h1>
      <p class="lead" style="margin:1.3rem auto 0;max-width:40rem;">ShedOS is an operating system for software developers. It ships a tiling Hyprland desktop and a complete development environment, already configured — and it treats the machine as something you can change freely and always take back.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- why it exists -->
  <section class="section bordered">
    <div class="container measure" style="text-align:center;">
      <span class="eyebrow no-rule" style="justify-content:center;">Why it exists</span>
      <h2 style="margin-top:.9rem;font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3.5vw,2.2rem);">A workstation shouldn't fight you.</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1.2rem;font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.7;">It should be ready the moment it boots, keep the configuration you give it, and recover when something goes wrong. Most systems manage one of those. ShedOS is built for all three: the desktop and toolchain come configured, your edits survive upgrades instead of being overwritten, and every upgrade is a snapshot you can undo in one command. A machine that fails to reach the desktop several times in a row even rolls itself back to the last working state — no rescue USB required.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- what's in the box -->
  <Section surface>
    <div class="section-head center">
      <span class="eyebrow">In the box</span>
      <h2>Everything a dev box needs, day one.</h2>
      <p>No three-weekend setup. The first <code class="code-inline">git clone</code> of your day is the first command that isn't already done for you.</p>
    </div>
    <CardGrid cols={3}>
      <article class="card centered">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/><path d="M3 9h18M9 9v12"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Tiling desktop</h3>
        <p>Hyprland on Wayland — waybar, mako, walker, gestures, and a themed lock screen, configured.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card centered">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m9 8-4 4 4 4M15 8l4 4-4 4"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Editors &amp; shell</h3>
        <p>Neovim on LazyVim, VS Code, and Bash with a fast starship prompt — tuned out of the box.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card centered">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 2v20M2 7l10 5 10-5M2 17l10 5 10-5"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Language runtimes</h3>
        <p>Python, Node, Go, Rust, and C++ — managed per project with mise, ready to build.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card centered">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 8h18v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2zM3 8l2-4h14l2 4M8 4v4M16 4v4"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Containers</h3>
        <p>Docker and the Kubernetes toolkit — kubectl, minikube, and helm — installed and running.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card centered">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 3l8 3v6c0 5-3.5 8-8 9-4.5-1-8-4-8-9V6l8-3zM9 12l2 2 4-4"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Resilient storage</h3>
        <p>A Btrfs root with automatic snapshots, plus LUKS full-disk encryption on by default.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card centered">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2"/><path d="m7 9 3 3-3 3M13 15h4"/></svg></div>
        <h3>One CLI: shedman</h3>
        <p>Updates, rollback, config review, theming, health, and more — one tool, each with a man page.</p>
      </article>
    </CardGrid>
  </Section>

  <!-- open source -->
  <Section>
    <div class="cta-band grid-bg">
      <span class="eyebrow no-rule" style="justify-content:center;">Open source</span>
      <h2 style="margin-top:.7rem;">Built in the open, GPL-3.0.</h2>
      <p>The whole system — packages, installer, desktop, and this site — lives in one repository. Issues and pull requests welcome.</p>
      <div class="hero-cta" style="justify-content:center;">
        <a href="https://github.com/Theshedman/shedos" class="btn btn-primary" rel="noopener">Source on GitHub</a>
        <a href="/community" class="btn btn-ghost">Community</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

</BaseLayout>
